From 427780bbc0fc524f8091893614eae8a653518139 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SteveDeFacto <5148995+SteveDeFacto@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 20:40:46 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Host services cold start: zero-app privacy agent behind the
 platform host policy, guarded bundles, locked package inputs

A host with no app yet can run its own public service roles: runPrivacy accepts
an empty app list only with a hostServices block that passes preflight and an
enabled platform host policy, and host services (any app count) start only on
the gate's authenticated admit, close on a refusal (ban, allowlist miss,
deregistration) and restart on the admin's admit. An empty list without a
usable block is refused as before. App-less hosts skip the per-round lease
read.

Enrollment: the operator's ENCLAVE_HOST_SERVICES_FILE opt-in is the only way a
fresh box can opt in; an app-less config is written only for a valid block the
agent would accept (worker staged, runner = keccak(endpoint), policy on) while
the node's own gate does not refuse the host. The first app joins by reload.

Bundles: the privacy agent is bundled from a main-guarded entry (a challenge
replica with policy carriers loaded host-services/runner.mjs, whose CLI exited
the agent); the consumer dns.mjs uses the route-dns argv-guard entry (it ran
the host-identity CLI); both builders refuse a bundle that does not parse or
carries a second main-module check.

Packages: every npm input must match its governing lockfile, and the gitignored
network-runtime bundle input must be exactly what this tree builds.

PrivacyAgent.start: a stop during the last startup status write no longer
leaves five intervals running (the process never exited).
